# Tomik, Wielder of Law: "Affinity for planeswalkers" counts the planeswalkers its caster controls. Bot2 controls Wrenn and Six and
# Bot1 none, so Tomik ({1}{W}{B}) still costs three: two Moxen cannot pay for him (`Mana: short`), a
# third can. With his own Wrenn and Six Tomik costs only two (the other scenarios).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Tomik, Wielder of Law
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Wrenn and Six
Swamp x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Wrenn and Six.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Tomik, Wielder of Law.Cast(Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tomik, Wielder of Law.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Tomik, Wielder of Law
